==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/əˈstɪɡmətɪzm̩/|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
From {{prefix|a||t1=not|lang=en}} stem of {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|στίγμα||mark, point}} {{suffix||ism|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{label|en|optics}} A defect of a [[lens]] such that light rays coming from a point do not meet at a [[focal point]] so that the image is blurred.
# {{label|en|pathology}} A disorder of the vision, usually due to a misshapen [[cornea]], such that light does not focus correctly on the [[retina]] causing a blurred image.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|astigmia}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|astigmatic}}
* {{l|en|astigmatically}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|stigma}}
* {{l|en|stigmatize}}

